== 2.9 Chapter 2 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [A bank that collects deposits and lends to the public is a],
  [commercial bank],
  [development bank],
  [central bank],
  [merchant bank]
)

#mcq(2, [The bank that issues currency in Nigeria is the],
  [Bank of Industry],
  [Central Bank of Nigeria],
  [Federal Mortgage Bank],
  [Nigerian Exchange]
)

#mcq(3, [A current account is distinguished by],
  [payment on demand by cheque],
  [a passbook],
  [the highest rate of interest],
  [a fixed term]
)

#mcq(4, [The account that pays the highest rate of interest is the],
  [current account],
  [domiciliary account],
  [savings account],
  [fixed deposit]
)

#mcq(5, [A bank overdraft is],
  [a share issue],
  [a fixed deposit],
  [permission to draw beyond the balance up to a limit],
  [a loan credited to the account]
)

#mcq(6, [With a cash ratio of 20 per cent, the credit multiplier is],
  [2],
  [20],
  [4],
  [5]
)

#mcq(7, [With a cash ratio of 25 per cent, the credit multiplier is],
  [4],
  [2.5],
  [5],
  [25]
)

#mcq(8, [A new deposit of ₦50,000 with a cash ratio of 10 per cent can support total deposits of],
  [₦550,000],
  [₦250,000],
  [₦500,000],
  [₦50,000]
)

#mcq(9, [Using the figures above, credit created is],
  [₦500,000],
  [₦550,000],
  [₦250,000],
  [₦450,000]
)

#mcq(10, [A deposit of ₦200,000 with a cash ratio of 20 per cent supports total deposits of],
  [₦400,000],
  [₦800,000],
  [₦1,000,000],
  [₦1,200,000]
)

#mcq(11, [Credit creation is limited by],
  [the number of staff],
  [the size of the building],
  [the number of bank branches],
  [the cash ratio and leakages into cash and imports]
)

#mcq(12, [The lender of last resort in a banking system is the],
  [central bank],
  [deposit insurance corporation],
  [stock exchange],
  [largest commercial bank]
)

#mcq(13, [The central bank acts as banker to],
  [traders],
  [foreign tourists],
  [the public],
  [the government and the commercial banks]
)

#mcq(14, [Clearing inter-bank indebtedness is part of the central bank's role as],
  [banker to the banks],
  [lender of last resort],
  [supervisor],
  [issuer of currency]
)

#mcq(15, [Selling treasury bills in the open market],
  [has no effect],
  [increases the money supply],
  [reduces the money supply],
  [raises the cash ratio]
)

#mcq(16, [Raising the cash reserve ratio],
  [lowers interest rates],
  [expands credit],
  [increases exports],
  [reduces the credit multiplier]
)

#mcq(17, [The rate at which the central bank lends to commercial banks is the],
  [savings rate],
  [bank rate],
  [lending rate],
  [exchange rate]
)

#mcq(18, [Moral suasion as an instrument of monetary policy means],
  [selling securities],
  [using force],
  [raising the reserve ratio],
  [persuading the banks to follow a policy]
)

#mcq(19, [A standing order is an instruction],
  [by the payer to his bank to pay a fixed sum regularly],
  [by a bank to a customer],
  [to dishonour a cheque],
  [by the payee to collect]
)

#mcq(20, [A direct debit is an arrangement in which],
