  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Commercial banks deal with the public; merchant banks deal mainly with firms and large finance.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Only the central bank may issue notes and coins.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    A current account is a demand account, and it usually pays no interest.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The bank pays for the use of the money over a term, so the term deposit earns most.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The customer draws as needed and pays interest on the amount used.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Multiplier = 1 ÷ 0.20 = 5.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    1 ÷ 0.25 = 4.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    50,000 × 10 = ₦500,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Total deposits ₦500,000 less the original ₦50,000 = ₦450,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    200,000 × 5 = ₦1,000,000.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The ratio sets the multiplier; leakages reduce it in practice.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The central bank lends to a solvent bank in temporary difficulty.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    It holds government accounts and the banks' reserves.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Settling differences between banks is banking the banks.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The central bank takes cash out of the banks when it sells bills.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    A higher ratio leaves less of each deposit to lend.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The bank or discount rate is the central bank's price of money to the banks.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    It is voluntary restraint urged by the central bank.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Fixed amount, fixed interval, payer's instruction.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The payee starts each collection, and the amount may vary.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    A draft is the bank's own promise, so the money is certain.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The importer's bank promises to pay the exporter against shipping documents.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Currency issue is a central-bank monopoly.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Savings accounts use a passbook or card and often limit withdrawals.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The bank pays for the use of the money it lends out.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The margin is the bank's gross income from intermediation.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Development banks supply long-term project finance.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    They lend small sums, often without formal security.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Dearer credit reduces the demand for loans.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    The sum is frozen at the central bank, so it cannot be lent.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    It repays depositors, up to a limit, if a bank fails.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "A", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Deposits are money the bank owes its customers.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    A loan is money owed to the bank.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Banks exchange cheques there and settle the net difference.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    It steers credit by sector rather than by total volume.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "D", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    A lower ratio leaves more to lend, so the multiplier rises.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "B", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
    Liquid assets can be turned into cash quickly to meet withdrawals.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "C", dense: true, pad: 20.17pt)[
